From: LiuWei <sunflowers0607@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:09:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] claude: a stale lateID no longer has the next turn's late
 message told whole

In the interactive mode a call told to the client by itself waits for
its message, which is left out (lateID). lateID kept its value after
that message was done. On a later turn, a call is told by itself again
and its own message is then written, and the check "lateID != "" &&
len(awaited) > 0" read it as a message written after calls it didn't
have: those calls were dropped from awaited and the message was told
the client whole.

Before 9fdcb7c31 that told the message's calls a second time, and the
client (Claude Code) ran each of them twice. Since 9fdcb7c31 a call
already told is skipped there, so the client gets the message's
thinking and text again; when every call in it was told already, the
reply ends on stop_reason tool_use with no tool_use block, and the
turn's answer written after it isn't told.

Only the calls awaited as the left-out message began (owed) are given
up on now; a call told by itself since waits for the next message.

Tests (TestClaudeTUI*), red at c360d9d30, green here:
- CallsBeforeTheirMessagesTwoTurns: "third reply told toolu_b again []"
  (the late message's thinking told again).
- ProductionShape: three calls left out, then a turn of four, the
  first two told before their message is written.
- FourTurns, MessageReallyWithoutItsCall: last reply "" [] "tool_use".
- MessageWrittenWhileItsCallWaits: the reply never ended.
RetriedMessageWithNewCall passes on both and pins the give-up of a
call whose attempt was asked again.

Run: go1.26.10 linux/amd64, -tags nogui, no network but loopback:
go test -count=1 -run '^TestClaudeTUI.*$' ./internal/gateway/ ok
(35 passed); at c360d9d30 with these tests, the five above red.
